The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
st->regmap = devm_regmap_init_mmio(&pdev->dev, base, &axi_adc_regmap_config);
ret = regmap_write(st->regmap, ADI_AXI_REG_RSTN, 0);
ret = regmap_read(st->regmap, ADI_AXI_REG_VERSION, &ver);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the driver attempts to initialize the register map and perform read/write operations on the IP core registers without ensuring that the AXI clock is enabled. If the clock is not active, these operations can lead to undefined behavior or errors, as the necessary clock signal for operation is absent.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
clk = devm_clk_get_enabled(&pdev->dev, NULL);
if (IS_ERR(clk))
    return PTR_ERR(clk);
```
Reason:
The fix involves explicitly obtaining and enabling the AXI clock before accessing the IP core registers. This ensures that the clock is active, allowing safe and correct read/write operations on the registers, thus preventing the undefined behavior that arises from the clock being disabled.

